tt-station (0.12.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.12.0.
  * Mobile app parity: the iPhone app covers what the desktop app does.
  * Desktop apps for Mac and Linux, alongside the app the box serves.
  * Signed updates: a box installs only releases signed by a key it trusts,
    and says so (`signing_ready`) when it has none.
  * Roles and an audit log: owners and members, and a record of who did what.
  * Chip leasing for every workload: models, bring-ups, labs and resets all
    take their chips through gozer.
  * Terminals removed.
  * Any Tenstorrent box: the agent starts with no config (hostname as its
    name, port 8765), reports the chips tt-smi finds instead of assuming
    4xBH, and publishes its SSH host keys (`GET /ssh/host-keys`).

 -- Tenstorrent <software@tenstorrent.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:06:17 -0400

tt-station (0.11.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.11.0.
  * CLI renamed: /usr/bin/tt is now /usr/bin/tt-station. The old name belongs
    to Tenstorrent's official CLI (tenstorrent/tt-cli) and this package was
    shadowing it. No `tt` alias or compatibility symlink is shipped -- update
    any scripts that invoked `tt <verb>`.
  * agentd now leases its chips through gozer before running or resetting a
    device: it acquires with --owner-pid so a live agentd is never reaped as
    stale, adopts any lease left behind by a previous agentd process, and
    refuses a reset/run/reset-chips that would hit a neighbour's chips. New
    `GET /leases` route and `tt-station leases` (was `tt leases`) surface each
    chip's gozer state to the Mac app and CLI.
  * telemetry: report media/diffusion workloads (tt-media-inference-server)
    in the tt_toplike.inference stream as a `media` object, alongside the
    existing vLLM `serving` object.

 -- Tenstorrent <software@tenstorrent.com>  Fri, 14 Aug 2026 16:43:45 -0700

